---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import DiveInCta from '../components/DiveInCta.astro';
import { business as b } from '../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="The Studio: A Marsh-View Recording Sanctuary in St. Augustine | The Fish Tank Recordings"
  description="A recording studio raised above the St. Augustine marsh, down a private drive under Spanish moss, with a huge deck, an SSL Origin console and a FLEA U47. Since 2002."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'The Studio', path: '/studio/' }]}
>
  <PageHero eyebrow="About · The sanctuary" title="Where the music meets <em>the marsh.</em>"
    lede={`Down a winding private drive under Spanish moss, a few minutes and a world away from St. Augustine’s busier streets, The Fish Tank Recordings sits raised on stilts above the marsh. The tubes are warm, the coffee is on and the view runs for miles. Since ${b.founded}, it has served as a retreat where artists collaborate and reconnect with their music, and with a little quiet.`} />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="gallery">
        <img class="img img--wide g1" src="/images/control-room-wide.webp" alt="The Fish Tank Recordings control room with an SSL console and a wall of guitars" width="1080" height="607" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g2" src="/images/vocal-booth.webp" alt="The vocal booth at The Fish Tank Recordings" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g3" src="/images/live-room.webp" alt="The live room at The Fish Tank Recordings, with amps, drums and a red rug" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <img class="img g4" src="/images/manley-closeup.webp" alt="Close-up of Manley outboard gear with glowing VU meters" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt" id="rooms">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The rooms</p>
      <h2>Four rooms, <em>one record.</em></h2>
      <div class="rooms">
        <article><img class="img" src="/images/control-room.webp" alt="The control room with the SSL Origin console" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><h3>The Control Room</h3><p>An SSL Origin console into Pro Tools HD, with Shadow Hills, Elysia, API, Empirical Labs and A-Designs outboard and a wall of guitars.</p></article>
        <article><img class="img" src="/images/live-room.webp" alt="The live room with amps and drums" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><h3>The Live Room</h3><p>Built for a full band, with personal monitor mixes, drums, amps and a window to the outdoors. Also used for band rehearsal.</p></article>
        <article><img class="img" src="/images/vocal-booth.webp" alt="The vocal booth" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><h3>The Vocal Booth</h3><p>The FLEA U47 Next and a quiet, treated booth for vocals, voice-over and narration.</p></article>
        <article><div class="rooms__ph" role="img" aria-label="The deck over the St. Augustine marsh"><span>Photo coming</span></div><h3>The Deck</h3><p>A large deck over the marsh for breaks between takes, listening sessions and small acoustic showcases.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section touring" id="touring-artists">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">For touring artists</p>
        <h2>Playing St. Augustine? <em>Spend the off day here.</em></h2>
        <p class="lede">The St. Augustine Amphitheatre, named Billboard’s Top East Coast Amphitheater, has made this small coastal city a regular stop for headliners. The Fish Tank Recordings gives the artists who play it a private room about 15 minutes away, with parking for buses and vans: somewhere to rehearse, unwind and, if the mood strikes, record.</p>
        <ul class="touring__list">
          <li><strong>Rehearse</strong><span>Run the set or work up a new song in a live room built for a full band, with personal monitor mixes.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Relax</strong><span>A marsh-view deck at the end of a private drive, out of sight and away from venue traffic.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Record</strong><span>Cut the song you wrote on the bus while it’s fresh, with a producer who plays nearly every instrument on the record.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p><a class="btn" href="/touring-artists/">Touring artists: check a date →</a></p>
        <p class="touring__contact">Managers and tour staff: call or text Lucio at <a href={`tel:${b.phoneE164}`}>{b.phone}</a> or email <a href={`mailto:${b.email}?subject=Touring%20artist%20session`}>{b.email}</a>. Booked directly with Lucio.</p>
      </div>
      <img class="img" src="/images/live-room.webp" alt="The live room at The Fish Tank Recordings, set up for a band" width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap grid split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A sanctuary, <em>not a booking room.</em></h2>
        <p>Many studios are windowless rooms in industrial parks. The Fish Tank Recordings has a wide view of the St. Augustine marsh, with wading birds over the grass, the tide moving in and out, and long Florida sunsets.</p>
        <p>A large deck sits just outside the control room. Artists step out between takes to clear their heads or talk through a bridge, then go back in to track. For Rubino, that pace is the point: sessions here are built around connection, to the song, to the other people in the room and to the setting.</p>

        <h2>Built above <em>the waterline.</em></h2>
        <p>The room has earned its altitude. Rubino moved the studio to this waterfront lot in 2016, and that October Hurricane Matthew flooded it and took the equipment with it. He rebuilt, and in September 2017 Hurricane Irma flooded it again. The answer was to go up: the studio now occupies an elevated wing of a house on stilts, with the cars parked underneath and the marsh out back.</p>

        <h2>Built for <em>making records.</em></h2>
        <p>Rubino designed the studio as part of the creative process. Songs get written on the couch, vocals get coached in the live room, and records are tracked, mixed and mastered without leaving the property.</p>
        <p>The control room is built around an <strong>SSL Origin</strong> console feeding <strong>Pro Tools HD</strong>, with outboard from Shadow Hills, Elysia, API, Empirical Labs and A-Designs. The vocal chain starts with a <strong>FLEA U47 Next</strong>, a modern build of the classic Neumann U47 design, and Royer and AEA ribbon mics cover guitars and room sound. Personal monitor mixes let a five-piece band track together.</p>
        <p>The instrument collection includes a wall of basses (Fender P-Bass, Music Man StingRay fretless, Dingwall, Zon and a six-string), guitars from Collings, PRS and Taylor, an upright bass, a Dobro, a banjo-guitar and a Medicine Man drum kit.</p>
        <p><a href="/gear/">Full gear list →</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Visit</p>
        <h3>{b.street}<br />{b.city}, {b.region} {b.postal}</h3>
        <p>Private drive · marsh-view deck · sessions by appointment</p>
        <p>Recording from somewhere else? Rubino produces remotely too. Or fly in and record above the St. Augustine marsh.</p>
        <DiveInCta />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .rooms { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .rooms { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }
  @media (min-width: 1100px) { .rooms { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } }
  .rooms .img, .rooms__ph { aspect-ratio: 4/5; width: 100%; }
  .rooms__ph { border-radius: 6px; border: 1px dashed var(--line); background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 30%, rgba(111,179,168,.18), transparent 70%), var(--ink); display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .rooms__ph span { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .rooms h3 { margin: 1rem 0 .4rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .rooms p { margin: 0; font-size: .95rem; }
  .touring .grid { align-items: center; }
  .touring__list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2rem 0; display: grid; gap: 1.1rem; }
  .touring__list li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr; gap: 1rem; padding-bottom: 1.1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .touring__list strong { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--amber); font-weight: 400; padding-top: .25rem; }
  .touring__contact { font-size: .95rem; }
  .gallery { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  .g1 { grid-column: 1 / -1; aspect-ratio: 21/9; }
  .g2, .g3, .g4 { aspect-ratio: 4/5; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .gallery { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .g1 { aspect-ratio: 16/10; } }
</style>
